WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:05.910
Slow breathing helps your body relax, and can ease your blood pressure. Here's how to do it.

00:06.410 --> 00:12.530
Sit comfortably, with your back supported and your feet flat on the floor. Rest one hand on your belly.

00:13.030 --> 00:22.340
Breathe in gently through your nose, for four counts. One. Two. Three. Four.

00:22.840 --> 00:35.780
Now breathe out slowly, through your mouth, for six counts. One. Two. Three. Four. Five. Six.

00:36.280 --> 00:42.330
Feel your belly rise as you breathe in, and fall as you breathe out. Keep your shoulders relaxed.

00:42.830 --> 00:58.640
Once more. Breathe in. Two. Three. Four. And out. Two. Three. Four. Five. Six.

00:59.140 --> 01:09.140
Practise for two minutes, twice a day. Just before you check your blood pressure is a good time too. If you feel light-headed, go back to normal breathing.
